# Pin golden fixture text files to LF line endings.
#
# Why: `cargo check` invokes `include_str!` at compile time, which
# embeds the bytes as they sit on disk. When a developer's
# `core.autocrlf` is `true` (the Windows default), the file is
# converted to CRLF on checkout — so the embedded bytes are CRLF.
# The renderer under test, by contrast, emits LF. The two diverge
# in line count and the golden-tree assertion fires
# (`browser::page_state::build::tests::
# the_thirteen_node_fixture_renders_the_golden_tree`).
#
# Fixing at the file level (eol=lf) means the bytes match
# regardless of checkout config; the commit message on the
# follow-up fix records the same finding.
#
# No other .txt in the repo is consumed as test data, so a
# blanket rule would be wider than the bug. Add new fixtures
# here as they appear.
src/browser/page_state/fixtures/*.golden.txt  text eol=lf